{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"standardConversion","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"for","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"standard","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PitchStandard","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/PitchStandard","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning13PitchStandardV"},{"text":") -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"PitchClass","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/PitchClass","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning10PitchClassV"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedInterval","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/DirectedInterval","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning16DirectedIntervalV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Ratio","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/Ratio","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning5RatioV"},{"text":">]?","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The reference pitch and its associated frequency.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"standard"}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A 35-entry dictionary, or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" if standard notation is not supported.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Returns ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" if this tuning system does not support standard pitch notation (e.g., because","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its interval of equivalence is not 2:1, or it has more than 35 distinct pitch classes per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"octave). Otherwise returns a dictionary with exactly 35 entries — one per pitch class.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Convention for each entry:"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" the directed frequency ratio from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"standard"},{"type":"text","text":"’s reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pitch to the instance of that pitch class within the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"same SPN octave","type":"text"}]},{"text":" as the reference.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Direction is ","type":"text"},{"code":".ascending","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if that same-octave instance lies above the reference,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".descending","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if below, and ","type":"text"},{"code":".same","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if it is the reference (or enharmonically equivalent).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For example, with A4 as the reference, every entry corresponds to a pitch in the range","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[C4, B4]. B maps to the ascending ratio to B4 — not to the nearer descending ratio to B3.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This same-SPN-octave rule holds for all pitch classes, regardless of chromatic distance","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the reference, and regardless of which pitch class is chosen as the reference.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}],"externalID":"s:10IvorTuning0B6SystemP18standardConversion3forSDyAA10PitchClassVAA16DirectedIntervalVyAA5RatioVGGSgAA0G8StandardV_tF","required":true,"title":"standardConve